<figure class="cache-figure" data-cache-access>
 <p class="figure-title">A command must pass both permission checks</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Request by cache-app <select data-request><option value="catalog">GET cache:catalog:42</option><option value="orders">GET cache:orders:42</option><option value="set">SET cache:catalog:42 12</option><option value="config">CONFIG GET maxmemory</option><option value="flush">FLUSHALL</option></select></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Simplified data policy: GET, SET, DEL, PING · keys matching cache:catalog:*</p>
 <div class="ops-access-path"><div data-command-gate><b>Command allowed?</b><strong data-command-result></strong></div><span>↓</span><div data-key-gate><b>Key allowed?</b><strong data-key-result></strong></div><span>↓</span><div data-outcome><b>Redis outcome</b><strong data-result></strong></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>A model of the lab’s simple allowlist, not a complete ACL interpreter or the server’s internal evaluation order. An authenticated application connection is assumed. Keyless commands have no key check to pass, but still need command permission. Network access, transport protection and end-user authorisation are separate boundaries.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{accessCases,accessDecision}from'../../lib/caching/operations.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-access]').forEach(root=>{const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-request]')!;const render=()=>{const request=accessCases[select.value],s=accessDecision(request);root.querySelector('[data-command-result]')!.textContent=s.commandAllowed?'Yes':'No';root.querySelector('[data-key-result]')!.textContent=request.key===null?'No key argument':s.keyAllowed?'Yes':'No';root.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=s.allowed?'Permitted':'NOPERM';root.querySelector('[data-command-gate]')!.classList.toggle('denied',!s.commandAllowed);root.querySelector('[data-key-gate]')!.classList.toggle('denied',!s.keyAllowed);root.querySelector('[data-outcome]')!.classList.toggle('denied',!s.allowed);root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.allowed?'The application can use this command on this namespace. Redis does not know which end user may view this product; the application must still enforce that decision.':!s.commandAllowed?'The namespace restriction does not make an administrative command safe. This identity has no permission to run it.':'GET is allowed, but this key belongs to the orders namespace. Command permission alone is insufficient.';};select.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
